# Suite runner-process (plan 04-20, D-20, D-21, D-23, D-32): tests/runner-process-tap.sh runs the
# real ivs-run of each preset.
# runner-process.scenario.<id>: one case per line of data/expected/runner-scenarios.ids (exit
#   code, outcome, exit.code, outcome.detail, `ivsr 3` first and `report.end <n>` last);
#   needs-user-exec needs an operator EXEC the gate never has and is a visible skip; since plan 07-10
#   (D-31) so is owner-exec-title, the template of the owner-local route (docs/owner-images.md), and the
#   gate prints one `-- SKIPPED <preset>/<suite>/<id>: <reason>` line per skipped id and preset.
# runner-process.mutant.<ID>: one case per program mutation of data/expected/diag-mutations.ids,
#   guest-fail naming its clause (D-32), and (plan 05-11) one per row of
#   data/expected/diag-mutations-ctrl-psg.ids, judged by the outcome and exit code of the row
#   (guest-fail 10, timeout 11, pass 0).
# runner-process.repeat.<id>, runner-process.slices.<id> (--slice-ticks 1 and 7) and
#   runner-process.cwd (run from another directory): byte-equal reports apart from host.calls;
#   the slicing, repeat and directory variants cover diag-boot-pass, diag-input-pass and, since plan
#   05-11 (cost cap V-16), diag-ctrl-psg-pass (runner-process.cwd.diag-ctrl-psg-pass).
# Plan 07-07 (D-23, D-06, A-16): the four scenarios demo-lamp-tone-{pass,idle,shift,swap} are scenario cases;
#   runner-process.repeat/slices/cwd.demo-lamp-tone-pass repeat the pass scenario only (cost cap);
#   runner-process.pair.<idA>.<idB>: the metamorphic judge, one case per line of data/expected/scenario-pairs.ids (two reports of the
#   same run related by differ and equal keys, input.consumed equal to input.events, an idle run silent);
#   runner-process.judge.pair-video-equal, .input-not-consumed and .idle-audible: fake report pairs that the pair judge must reject.
# Plan 07-08 (D-25, A-14, A-17): runner-process.mutant.SCN-*, one case per row of data/expected/diag-mutations-scn.ids (12 mutants and one
#   negative row of the Lamp Tone program; stub-window rows patch boot-stub-2.exec; a fails column states the complete failing set).
# Plan 07-11 (D-31, T-07-29): runner-process.refuse-user.audio-raw, .psg-log-out and .audio-wav: each option is refused for a scenario with a
#   `content ... user` line (exit 14, one stderr line `<option> refused: content user`, no report, no file).
# Plan 07-11 (D-31, T-07-26 to T-07-28): runner-process.owner-run.<case>, the nine cases of the owner-local helper tools/owner-run.sh (usage,
#   ci-env, github-actions-env, in-tree-path, wrong-size, missing-lock, bad-lock-line, no-images-skip, identity-mismatch), each on a copy of the
#   helper in a scratch root outside the work tree with project-made zero-filled files only; runner-process.judge.owner-run-refusal rejects a
#   fake helper that exits 0 where it must refuse.
# runner-process.judge.<slug>: judge self-controls, each passing only when the judge fails a fake
#   runner for its intended reason (exit code, missing report.end, outcome and exit.code
#   disagreeing, a changed report body; plan 04-24: a removed demonstrating scenario).
# runner-process.outcomes-consistent: --help, docs/runner.md and data/expected/runner-outcomes.ids
#   agree; runner-process.outcomes-covered: every outcome has a running scenario.
# runner-process.watchdog: the watchdog self-control (stopped at once it stays silent; it stops a
#   run past its limit).
